1
00:00:14,881 --> 00:00:15,682
Good evening.

2
00:00:15,723 --> 00:00:17,686
I trust you had a fruitful day.

3
00:00:17,887 --> 00:00:19,068
I do not say happy.

4
00:00:19,088 --> 00:00:21,013
I hope it has been happy.

5
00:00:21,053 --> 00:00:38,204
Namo Tassa Bhagavato Arahato Sambha Sambhodassa Namo Tassa Bhagavato Arahato Sambha Sambhodassa

6
00:00:38,927 --> 00:00:47,279
Naotasa bhagavato arahato samma sambuddhasa.

7
00:00:47,979 --> 00:00:55,609
Homage to the Buddha, the blessed noble and fully self-awakened one.

8
00:00:55,649 --> 00:00:58,573
So we had a bit of magic yesterday.

9
00:00:59,161 --> 00:01:07,454
But I just love the way the Buddha sort of brings it, grounds it into I'm aware of feelings, aware of perceptions and so on.

10
00:01:08,055 --> 00:01:25,724
And if you were to choose one word which expresses the whole purpose of the Buddhist practice, it would be to discover the nature of sati-awareness, satipañña, intuitive awareness.

11
00:01:27,140 --> 00:01:35,409
So now this discourse, the Bhūmija Sutta, the Bhūmija discourse, is concerned with aspiration.

12
00:01:36,930 --> 00:01:47,804
And we have here the quadrilemma, if you remember, to be, not to be, both to be and not to be, and this wonderful neither to be nor not to be.

13
00:01:48,265 --> 00:01:51,087
So we're using that for a different purpose here.

14
00:01:53,481 --> 00:02:14,814
so this is uh the buddha's back in raj gear which is the capital of uh bimbisara on the on this uh sitting on the um ganges and uh with uh a venerable bumija is uh going his realms and he meets uh prince jayasena and he seems to be an uncle of this prince

15
00:02:15,942 --> 00:02:29,341
And when the prince sees him, the usual courteous and amiable talk, and then he says, there are some recluses and Brahmins who make such assertions and hold such views as this.

16
00:02:30,502 --> 00:02:42,860
If one makes an aspiration and one leaves the holy life by which is meant here, the monastic life or the celibate life, one is unable to procure any fruit.

17
00:02:43,802 --> 00:02:49,393
If one makes no aspiration, one is not able to procure any fruit.

18
00:02:50,114 --> 00:03:08,105
If you make an aspiration and then you make no aspiration, remember both of them, make an aspiration and not make an aspiration, and lead the holy life, you're unable to procure the fruit.

19
00:03:08,086 --> 00:03:25,402
and if neither makes an aspiration nor makes no aspiration and leaves the holy life one is unable to procure any fruit now even though i've said this is the monastic life actually as we will see is basically the eightfold power

20
00:03:28,066 --> 00:03:38,424
Now, what Bumager says is, or answers, I've not heard or learned that from the Blessed One's own lips, Prince, but it is possible that the Blessed One might say thus.

21
00:03:39,265 --> 00:03:44,455
If one makes an aspiration and one leads the holy life unwisely,

22
00:03:44,435 --> 00:04:13,817
one is unable to procure any fruit and so he goes through the four of them so you know it makes no aspiration and leaves the holy life unwisely then one will not procure any fruit there won't be a good outcome and so it is with one who makes an aspiration and makes no aspiration or neither makes an aspiration nor not makes an aspiration so they um they won't make it however he says

23
00:04:14,421 --> 00:04:38,555
uh if one makes an aspiration and leaves the holy life wisely then one will procure fruit and so he goes through the quadrilemma so the the difference here is an aspiration and to lead the holy life in a wise way now i've not learnt this from the blessed one's own lips but it is possible that the blessed one would answer as i have stated

24
00:04:39,802 --> 00:04:56,805
Now, and the prince, now if Boomergers, if your, if Master Boomerger's teacher speaks thus, if he declares thus, then it certainly seems that the venerable Boomerger's teacher stands ahead of all the ordinary recluses and Brahmins.

25
00:04:58,067 --> 00:05:06,298
So, and then Prince Jatena served the venerable one from his own dish of milk rice, which was a bit of a delicacy.

26
00:05:07,762 --> 00:05:14,377
And after his alms round, etc., Bhumija went back to the monastery and there was the Buddha.

27
00:05:15,500 --> 00:05:21,233
And this is what he said, of course, to the Blessed One.

28
00:05:22,444 --> 00:05:26,029
I hope, having told him, he said, I hope I've answered as you would have answered.

29
00:05:26,810 --> 00:05:33,139
I said what has been said by the Blessed One and did not misrepresent him with what is concrete to fact.

30
00:05:33,300 --> 00:05:34,201
So that's what he's hoping.

31
00:05:34,862 --> 00:05:38,887
And then there's this lovely sentence that we've had before in many discourses.

32
00:05:39,108 --> 00:05:48,081
I hope I explained in accordance with the Dharma in such a way that nothing which provides a ground for censure

33
00:05:48,685 --> 00:05:53,014
can be legitimately deduced from my assertion.

34
00:05:55,360 --> 00:06:00,350
Yeah, I just find that sentence rather chuckling.

35
00:06:00,370 --> 00:06:07,706
Now, the Buddha replies, oh, absolutely, surely, surely, you've answered as I would have answered in so many words, you see.

36
00:06:08,817 --> 00:06:20,473
And then the Buddha says when recluses and Brahmins have a wrong view, wrong intention, wrong speech, wrong action, wrong livelihood, wrong effort, wrong mindfulness and wrong concentration.

37
00:06:20,795 --> 00:06:22,357
So there's your Eightfold Path.

38
00:06:22,918 --> 00:06:27,805
If they make an aspiration and they lead the holy life, they're unable to procure the fruit.

39
00:06:27,785 --> 00:06:30,728
So an aspiration, a desire.

40
00:06:30,788 --> 00:06:37,076
So one joins an order or one joins the practice of Buddhism with an aspiration.

41
00:06:37,497 --> 00:06:49,954
It might be a simple aspiration to lead a more easy life, to try and overcome one's anxieties and angers and all that sort of stuff.

42
00:06:49,973 --> 00:06:52,398
It can be just on that very simple basis.

43
00:06:52,978 --> 00:06:55,040
It could be to improve relationships.

44
00:06:55,307 --> 00:07:04,060
And it could have this far-reaching aspiration to become fully liberated from all suffering, to achieve nibbāna.

45
00:07:07,425 --> 00:07:16,016
But here he says that if you're not on the right path, it's an absolute waste of time.

46
00:07:17,194 --> 00:07:23,053
because he says the wrong path is not a proper method for procuring fruit.

47
00:07:23,656 --> 00:07:29,415
Okay, so now we have these usual metaphors to try and get this across.

48
00:07:30,069 --> 00:07:42,209
Supposing a man needing oil, seeking oil, wandering in search of oil, were to heap up gravel in a tub, sprinkle it all over with water and press it.

49
00:07:42,951 --> 00:07:47,838
And if he'd made an aspiration and acted thus, he would be unable to procure any oil.

50
00:07:48,521 --> 00:07:50,142
And then he goes through the quadrilemma.

51
00:07:50,504 --> 00:07:55,992
If he hadn't, if he both had and hadn't, and if he neither had nor hadn't.

52
00:07:57,137 --> 00:08:00,747
Because it's not the proper method for procuring oil.

53
00:08:00,807 --> 00:08:13,442
Now suppose a man needing milk, seeking milk, wandering in search of milk were to pull a recently carved cow by the horn, thinking to milk her by the horn.

54
00:08:13,826 --> 00:08:31,209
Well, of course, he made an aspiration, I want milk, and he'd gone through the quadrilateral, he made no aspiration, and so on, but he still pulled on the horn, then this is not the proper method for procuring milk, and therefore there'd be no fruit.

55
00:08:33,812 --> 00:08:43,563
Supposing a man needing butter, seeking butter, wandering in search of butter, were to pour water into a churn and churn it with a churning stick,

56
00:08:44,067 --> 00:08:59,173
Now he made an aspiration, you know, I want butter, but of course all the ingredients are wrong and the methodology is not quite right and therefore this is not the proper method for procuring butter and he would of course be disappointed.

57
00:09:00,553 --> 00:09:28,400
Supposing a man needing fire, seeking fire, wandering in search of fire, were to take an upper fire stick and rub a wet, sappy piece of wood with it, then no matter whether he made an aspiration or not, both aspiration and no aspiration, or neither an aspiration nor not an aspiration, then because it's not the proper method of procuring fire, he would not get what he wants.

58
00:09:31,604 --> 00:09:34,107
Now, the opposite now, of course, is true.

59
00:09:34,148 --> 00:09:51,232
Those recluses and Brahmins who have right view, right intention, right speech, right action, right livelihood, right effort, right mindfulness and right concentration, if they make an aspiration and lead the holy life, they are able to procure fruit.

60
00:09:51,653 --> 00:09:57,121
Now, even if you don't make an aspiration, but you lead the good life, right,

61
00:09:57,557 --> 00:10:00,863
Then they are able to procure fruit.

62
00:10:01,144 --> 00:10:08,215
So this means that you might say to yourself, I'm doing this for this reason.

63
00:10:08,274 --> 00:10:14,605
And because you're following the right path, you should bear some fruit.

64
00:10:14,938 --> 00:10:26,054
But even if you had a sort of hazy idea of what you wanted or didn't want anything in particular, but you led the good life, here the holy life, remember, is the Eightfold Path.

65
00:10:26,096 --> 00:10:28,519
Well, we're all following the Eightfold Path.

66
00:10:28,538 --> 00:10:36,791
So if you lead the good life without any particular aspiration, just that will lead you to a good result.

67
00:10:37,491 --> 00:10:41,317
Now, this reminds me of sailors going down

68
00:10:41,618 --> 00:10:56,386
down the side of Africa and often they would come across the doldrums and the doldrums were the places where there was no wind so that the ship would seem to be just stuck in the middle of the ocean

69
00:10:56,957 --> 00:11:20,129
and it was a frightening time obviously for sailors but unwittingly of course the flow of the ocean was gently carrying them down the side of africa so that's what i i understand by this that even though a person doesn't have any particular aspiration uh doesn't particularly want anything from the practice but still does the practice

70
00:11:20,110 --> 00:11:30,592
With right view, right action, right livelihood, etc., etc., that will gently carry them down the path of enlightenment or awakening.

71
00:11:33,138 --> 00:12:01,153
so now of course we have the uh we have the metaphors needing oil seeking oil wandering in search of oil were to heap up sesamum seed sesamum flower in a tub sprinkle it all over and press it so this is how you get oil from sesamums from sesamum flower so there's a little uh a little trick for you so and of course because he uh he's done a right method then he'll he'll bear the fruit

72
00:12:01,605 --> 00:12:07,135
even though he makes no aspiration or neither makes no aspiration nor no aspiration.

73
00:12:08,118 --> 00:12:08,839
Same with milk.

74
00:12:08,938 --> 00:12:14,808
Needing milk, seeking milk, wandering in search of milk were to pull a recently carved cow by her udder.

75
00:12:15,370 --> 00:12:17,995
Then, of course, he would have the milk.

76
00:12:19,256 --> 00:12:29,447
And then suppose a man needing butter, seeking butter, wandering in search of butter, were to pour curd into a churn and churn it with a churning stick.

77
00:12:29,969 --> 00:12:45,304
Then, because he'd made the aspiration, if he made no aspiration, if he both made an aspiration and made no aspiration, and if he neither made an aspiration nor made no aspiration and acted thus, he would still be able to procure butter.

78
00:12:45,466 --> 00:12:46,767
So that's the point, you see.

79
00:12:49,361 --> 00:13:01,735
why because it's the proper method supposing a man needing fire seeking fire wandering in search of fire were to make the upper fire stick and rubber dry sapless piece of wood with it

80
00:13:02,102 --> 00:13:27,148
then if he made the aspiration or even if he made no aspiration though it's a bit difficult to think that you go to the trouble of rubbing sticks with aspiration to make fire but even so and if both made an aspiration uh or made no aspiration neither made an aspiration nor no aspiration and acted upon it he would thus be able to procure fire why is that because this is the proper method for procuring fire

81
00:13:28,477 --> 00:13:42,461
Now the Buddha says, Bhoomija, if these four similes had occurred to you with reference to Prince Jayasena, he would have spontaneously acquired confidence in you and being confident would have shown his confidence in you.

82
00:13:43,621 --> 00:13:45,205
So this is...

83
00:13:46,837 --> 00:13:55,518
I know this is still an age where stories, metaphors, ideas can have seemingly a great effect on people.

84
00:13:56,620 --> 00:13:59,548
I'm not so sure that works for us these days so much.

85
00:13:59,607 --> 00:14:04,779
We're so scientific, inverted commas, you know, so logical and precise.

86
00:14:06,227 --> 00:14:21,701
And Venerable Sir, says Bhumijo, how could these similes have occurred to me with reference to Prince Jayasena, as they occur to the Blessed One, since they are spontaneous and have never been heard before?

87
00:14:21,761 --> 00:14:35,374
So I think we can take it that the Buddha was very good at offering these images, these similes, these metaphors to balance the sort of dry explanation of his teachings.

88
00:14:36,738 --> 00:14:44,128
This is what the Blessed One said, and the Venerable Bhumija was satisfied and, of course, delighted in the Blessed One's words.

89
00:14:44,970 --> 00:14:51,217
So I think there's an interesting point there about aspiration.

90
00:14:52,740 --> 00:14:57,147
If we just follow the path, then that will take us.

91
00:14:57,606 --> 00:15:00,350
And it sort of reminds me, really, of beginner's mind.

92
00:15:00,510 --> 00:15:02,374
This is the great Zen saying.

93
00:15:02,692 --> 00:15:09,841
where a person comes into the practice with no idea, no idea at all.

94
00:15:09,900 --> 00:15:11,884
That was similar to me, really.

95
00:15:12,403 --> 00:15:23,357
And because you've got no idea and because you've got no big aim, you just do the practice as a beginner with wide eyes and an open mouth.

96
00:15:24,379 --> 00:15:29,546
Then, of course, you get the benefit of the practice because the practice itself is what's doing the work.

97
00:15:31,428 --> 00:15:32,529
So anyway, I hope

98
00:15:32,914 --> 00:15:49,960
This discourse will have inspired you not to make too many aspirations, not to worry whether you have an aspiration or not, and that you will continue following the Eightfold Path and become fully liberated from all suffering sooner rather than later.

99
00:15:51,621 --> 00:15:52,864
Now we can do a little practice.

